# cloakai/dev
#
# Cloakai agent image.
#
# Run:    docker run ... $(cat agents/isolation-flags) cloakai/dev run "prompt"
# Shell:  docker run ... $(cat agents/isolation-flags) cloakai/dev shell
# MCP:    docker run ... $(cat agents/isolation-flags) cloakai/dev mcp
#
# This is a WORD LIST for shell word-splitting. The mount is deliberately NOT
# here: it depends on the caller's project directory, so it is passed separately.
#
# Every flag below is required, and each was derived by escalating one at a time
# and reading the next failure — see docs/verification/phase-0.md Check 3. None is
# cargo-cult. If you add a flag, add the reason.
#
#   --network      comes from the caller (cloakai-internal). There is no fallback:
#                  an accidental default-bridge attachment is an open container.
#
#   --read-only    the root filesystem is the isolation boundary.
#
#   The four --tmpfs mounts are each REQUIRED, discovered one at a time by
#   reading the next EROFS. Under --read-only the agent writes to /root/.local,
#   then /root/.config, then /root/.cache. A whole writable $HOME is not needed,
#   and three isolated subdirectories keep nothing persistent between runs.
#
#   --cap-drop=ALL / no-new-privileges   no privilege escalation from inside.
#
#   --pids-limit / --memory / --cpus     resource ceilings. Phase 0 confirmed 64
#                  pids and 512m also complete a real model call, so these are
#                  conservative rather than tight.
#
#   NOT HERE, deliberately:
#     --privileged            never. Root-equivalent on the host.
#     -v /var/run/docker.sock never. Lets the agent start sibling containers,
#                             which defeats the entire isolation model.
#     any second bind mount  the project directory is the one intentional
#                             exception, scoped by choice and discipline, not by
#                             anything the spec enforces.
--network NETWORK_PLACEHOLDER
--read-only
--tmpfs /tmp
--tmpfs /root/.local
--tmpfs /root/.config
--tmpfs /root/.cache
--cap-drop=ALL
--security-opt no-new-privileges
--pids-limit=1024
--memory=4g
--cpus=2
